journal_verdicts.cell:cross-domain:
G1 is worth its ~2.5 GPU-h, but as the dossier states it, it cannot tell what a pass or a fail means. Methods from outside the field supply mostly budget-neutral fixes; the only extra cost is a few inference-only probes.

The largest problem is identification. With 3 SWA-512 layers, attention alone can relay a fact up to 3×512 = 1,536 tokens (Mistral, arXiv 2310.06825). Models trained with SWA are measured doing exactly this past the window (2609.34049). So a fact 512 tokens back is not state-only. Gate on a bin more than 1,536 tokens back; it fits the 2,048-token context. Report the under-512 and 512-1,536 bins as well, add a v=0 fact-write ablation as a causal check, and put a preamble before the facts so they cannot leak through attention-sink positions.

The second problem is measurement. The 4-digit exact match is a discontinuous metric (2304.15004), so a single-seed read at one learning rate at 134M cannot separate four explanations of a fail:
- the gates do not retain: fla's default initialisation gives only about 2.6% of heads a timescale over 512 tokens;
- there is no shared cross-lingual representation: at this model shape, cross-script bitext retrieval sits at 5.5-7% without coherent bilingual context (2609.30535);
- the learning rate was not tuned (2608.11859);
- noise.

Budget-neutral fixes:
- **Schedule:** one constant-rate trunk to 1B tokens, with a 20% cooldown branch for the 200M read (2405.18392). This saves ~0.16 GPU-h, which pays for a 3-value learning-rate sweep at about 50M tokens each.
- **Continuous readouts:** per-digit accuracy, correct-code log-probability and rank among the N codes, next to the exact-match gate.
- **Error bar:** noise from the last few checkpoints (2508.13144).
- **Per checkpoint, inference only:**
  - CSLS bitext retrieval on FLORES+ dev for the residual stream and the GDN write; CKA reported but not decisive;
  - a beyond-reach in-context-learning loss gap, after 2209.11895;
  - per-head decay timescales;
  - a language-identity probe;
  - A0's own write equivariance, which sizes how much room the later A1 loss has.
- **Reporting:** per language pair and same-script vs cross-script.
- **Pre-registered rules:** a fail with a loss spike triggers a second seed (2503.09543); a fail at one untuned learning rate is INCONCLUSIVE; a chrono-style initialisation is a repair arm, never a silent change to A0.

Expect G1 to be hard. Pretrained Samba needed task fine-tuning before it could recall past the window (2406.07522), so the 5% recall curriculum is load-bearing. Evidence for later stages: LooC and SER (separate language subspace, choice of loss layers), Wu & Dredze (a documented null for explicit alignment losses) and Double Trouble (exposure matching). None of these changes G1's scope, and none of this is a novelty claim.

Novelty.strongest_argument:
Refuted on the recombination prong, not by a direct prior match. The gate says itself that it "claims no method novelty", and almost every piece of its measurement is already published, including its MONO line and both identification checks.

(1) The MONO line has been measured in close configurations.
- 2609.33093 (How Linear Attention Remembers) used released from-scratch pure GDN-340M checkpoints (m-a-p 340M-20B), where attention is structurally absent. It tested natural-text in-context recall of K facts at distances 128 to 1,024 tokens (Fig. 7). Recall was 47-60% at K=32 (Fig. 8). Blocking the fact-time write cut recall by 36-79 pp (Sec. 3), which is the same check as the registration's ABLATION. In the near-matched 3:1 hybrid the state carried under 1% (Sec. 4.1). App. F.2 even ran a prose-retrieval pilot with paraphrased queries: 56.3% top-1 at 512 filler tokens.
- SWAX (2509.24552) trained SWA plus xLSTM hybrids from scratch with window arms 128 to 2,048, including 512. It reasons explicitly about the O(lw) receptive field (Sec. 3: 128 x 24 = 3,072 tokens) and measures RULER NIAH far beyond it, out to 131K (Fig. 5). Fig. 6 decomposes recall by train-time versus test-time window.
- Griffin (2402.19427, Sec. 6.2) mixes local attention with a gated linear recurrence, trained from scratch. Its 7B model (300B tokens) solves phonebook retrieval up to the 1,024 local window and degrades beyond it. The proposal does not cite Griffin, and none of its 97 counted queries returned it, so this is a coverage gap.

(2) The identification devices are borrowed, as the proposal's own Novelty Ledger concedes:
- the state cut is 2610.06750's attention-only condition (also 2609.33093's state replacement and 2609.04434's split-prefill);
- the reach bound is the l x w receptive-field arithmetic of 2310.06825 and 2608.28444, which SWAX also applies;
- the binding margin is a standard distractor control.
The ledger itself rates A0 as occupied and the B3 bin as "a design detail, not a contribution".

(3) The one residual is swapping the repeated key for a surface-disjoint translation. That is the cross-lingual needle protocol of MLNeedle (2408.10151), OneRuler (2503.01996) and 2504.10906, all on dense models, dropped into the configuration in (1).

(4) The likely outcome is predicted by the proposal's own citations:
- 2504.10906: cross-lingual context retrieval comes from post-training, not pretraining scale;
- 2604.17633: translations without token overlap first appear at about 11B tokens in a 1.7B model;
- 2609.19291: activation alignment was null at 360M;
- Griffin: retrieval degrades beyond the window even at 7B;
- SWAX: long-range recall appears around 1.4B;
- the owner's own prior puts PASS at about 0.1.
So the combination adds little that its parts do not already predict. That is the lens's "trivial recombination" condition.

Procedural defect: the closest priors for the instrument row (MLNeedle, OneRuler) are marked "legacy citations, not re-read in this gauntlet". That breaks the orx rule (read with --full before writing a delta row), and the cap for incomplete novelty coverage is 74.

What survives: no paper I found measures cross-lingual in-context recall through a recurrent state with attention structurally excluded. This is NARROWED with the novelty cap, not a reject for direct-prior match.
